From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: the delete question shows the item as Windows does; the Recycle Bin lists each volume once

Under "Are you sure you want to move this file to the Recycle Bin?" (and
"permanently delete", "can't be moved", "too big") Windows shows the item: its
own icon (the extra large one, no question icon), its name, and for a file
"Type:", "Size:" and "Date modified:", for a folder "Date created:"; several
items get the question alone, with the bin's icon. We showed the item's full
path (9063). The details are also kept in the dialog's WINE_CONFIRM_ITEM
property beside WINE_CONFIRM. An item whose details can't be read keeps its
path under the question.

The Recycle Bin's Properties listed C: and Z: as two bin locations, although
C: is a folder of the Linux file system Z: is the root of. Windows lists
volumes: one location per file system now, under its first letter (a
drive's size and free space are its file system's, compared read at once).

Gates: make test-deleteask (new), make test-recyclebin (one location).
Mutants: -DSG_MUTANT_CONFIRM_NO_DETAILS, -DSG_MUTANT_RB_EVERY_LETTER.
